# Uber (Ride Matching Service)

# Monolith Archiecture

# Tech Stack
  - NodeJs
  - Express
  - Javascript
  - MongoDB
  - Redis
  - Socket (over pooling)

# Apis
  - auth
  - create ride request
  - Fare Estimation (exclude)
  - confirm booking
  - get nearby drivers
  - notify drivers
  - accept ride
  - eta calc(extact time to arrival)
  - start ride
  - complete ride
  - get ride history


# Flow
  - In real world a connection is made between driver and redis by using websocket or pooling or message queue (kafka or other)
  - driver -> updateLocation() -> redis + mongodb
  - passesnger -> createBooking()->nearByLocation() -> (radius 1km,2km,5km (defualt for now 5km)) -> redis -> notify -> accept/reject(confirmBooking) -> 


websocket - are like opening a persistent tunnel b/w client and server
, will be used for notifing ride requests


# xyz - createBooking();

# a,b,c - drivers online and d offline

# findNearByDrivers and get detials form db 

# Redis store
  - driver:a - socket(1) -> recieves msg (new ride request) -> confirmBooking
  - driver:b - socket(2)
  - driver:c - socket(3) -> -> recieves msg (as soon as a accepts the goes vanishes)

# Redis store for messaging/notifying
  - BookingId : [a,b,c]
  - keep [a] remove [b,c]

